From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christophe Branchereau <cbranchereau@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] meson: build the dril target on drm-only platforms

In 24.3 the DRI megadrivers moved to the new dril target, which is only
built when glx==dri or an X11/XCB platform is in use. Headless platforms
using EGL + gbm on KMS (e.g. buildroot configs without X.org) therefore
stopped getting any /usr/lib/dri driver plugins, leaving EGL and gbm
without a loadable driver.

Also allow building dril when the DRI platform is drm.

Signed-off-by: Christophe Branchereau <cbranchereau@proton.me>
---
 src/meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/meson.build b/src/meson.build
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -133,7 +133,7 @@
   subdir('egl')
 endif
 if with_gallium and with_gbm
-  if with_glx == 'dri' or with_platform_x11 or with_platform_xcb
+  if with_glx == 'dri' or with_platform_x11 or with_platform_xcb or with_dri_platform == 'drm'
     subdir('gallium/targets/dril')
   endif
 endif
